From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:23:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: log infoframe changes at debug level

nv_drm_atomic_check() printed an INFO line every time HDR metadata,
colorspace or the HDMI VSIF changed on a CRTC. It runs for TEST_ONLY
commits too, so compositors probing output configurations, for example
while turning HDR on, fill the kernel log with bursts of these lines.
Print it with DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER instead.

The format string also ended in "\n" although the logging macros already
add one, so every message was followed by an empty line. Drop it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
index 724581e2..ec805876 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
@@ -680,7 +680,7 @@ int nv_drm_atomic_check(struct drm_device *dev,
 
                 /* Check if HDR metadata or colorspace changed */
                 if (hdr_changed || colorspace_changed || vsif_metadata_changed) {
-                    NV_DRM_LOG_INFO("Infoframe changed on CRTC %d (hdr=%d colorspace=%d vsif=%d), adding planes on CRTC to atomic commit\n",
+                    NV_DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER("Infoframe changed on CRTC %d (hdr=%d colorspace=%d vsif=%d), adding planes on CRTC to atomic commit",
                            to_nv_crtc(crtc)->head,
                            hdr_changed,
                            colorspace_changed,
